n hand). W2, W7, W8 are W suit, and I already have some W tiles; keeping them might form a W chow later (W2,W4,W4,W7,W8 \u2014 possible chow W2,W3,W4 or W6,W7,W8). But with only 9 tiles left, chow formation is unlikely.  \n\nSo discard one of the isolated B tiles. B4 has 4 left unseen, very safe. B1 and B2 also safe. Choose B4 to keep B1,B2 which might pair or form chow together (B1,B2,B3).  \n\nReason:  \nDiscarding B4 maintains flexibility with W suit for possible chows, keeps the T6 pung and W4 pair, and is safe (many unseen). It doesn't reduce scoring potential significantly.  \n\nAnswer: Play B4"}
